# System Verification Guide: ESP32 AI Pet

This guide provides a structured approach to verify the hardware, firmware, and server integration of the Kaku Pet device.

## 1. System Architecture Flowchart

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start((Power ON)) --> HW_Init[<b>Hardware Initialization</b><br/>Serial, I2C, Camera, OLED]
    HW_Init --> Load_State[<b>Load State</b><br/>Restore Pet Stats from NVS]
    Load_State --> WiFi_Check{WiFi Credentials<br/>Found?}
    
    WiFi_Check -- No --> WiFi_Prov[<b>WiFi Provisioning</b><br/>Show QR Code on OLED]
    WiFi_Prov --> WiFi_Wait[Wait for Web Config]
    WiFi_Wait --> WiFi_Success[Save & Reboot]
    WiFi_Success --> Start
    
    WiFi_Check -- Yes --> WiFi_Connect[<b>WiFi Connection</b><br/>Connecting to Router]
    WiFi_Connect --> Net_Check{Connected?}
    
    Net_Check -- No --> Net_Retry[Retry Loop<br/>Backoff Delay]
    Net_Retry --> WiFi_Connect
    
    Net_Check -- Yes --> Init_Sync[<b>Initial Sync</b><br/>Poll Server for Events]
    Init_Sync --> Main_Loop[<b>Main Execution Loop</b>]
    
    subgraph Logic_Network [Core 1: Pet Brain & Comms]
        Main_Loop --> Phys_Tick{60s Tick?}
        Phys_Tick -- Yes --> Phys_Update[<b>Physiology Update</b><br/>Hunger++, Thirst++, Poop?]
        Phys_Tick -- No --> Net_Handler[<b>Network Task</b><br/>Process Queue / Poll Events]
        Net_Handler --> OTA_Proc{OTA Logic?}
        OTA_Proc -- Update Found --> OTA_Download[Download & Flash]
        OTA_Download --> Reboot[Reboot]
    end
    
    subgraph UI_Interaction [Core 0: UI & Sensors]
        Main_Loop --> Sensor_Poll[<b>Read Sensors</b><br/>MPU6050, Mic VAD]
        Sensor_Poll --> Orient_Logic{Orientation?}
        
        Orient_Logic -- Neutral --> Mood_IDLE[<b>Idle State</b><br/>Play State Animations]
        Orient_Logic -- Flat 2min --> Sleep_Mode[<b>Deep Sleep</b>]
        Orient_Logic -- Tilted --> Menu_Syst[<b>Interaction Menu</b>]
        
        Menu_Syst --> Nav{Menu Action?}
        Nav -- Right Hold --> Menu_Enter[Enter Menu]
        Nav -- Right Flick --> Menu_Next[Cycle Menus]
        Nav -- Left Hold --> Exec_Action[<b>Execute Action</b><br/>Feed, Clean, Play]
        
        Exec_Action --> Action_Effect[<b>Visual Feedback</b><br/>Action Animation]
        Action_Effect --> Notify_Server[<b>Sync Event</b><br/>Queue Server Update]
    end
```

---

## 2. Expected Behavior at Each Step

| Step | Expected Result |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Power ON** | Device boots; serial logs appear; OLED shows startup animation. |
| **WiFi Init** | If configured: Connects within 10s. If new: Shows QR code for provisioning. |
| **Idle State** | Pet animation (Infant/Child/etc.) plays. Happiness/Idle frames cycle every few seconds. |
| **Physiology Update** | Every 60s, internal stats (Hunger, Thirst) change. Uptime counter increments. |
| **Menu Cycle** | Right tilt flick cycles between Food, Toilet, Play, Health menus flawlessly. |
| **Action Execution** | Left tilt hold triggers specific animation (e.g., eating frames) and vibrates/sounds if enabled. |
| **Server Sync** | Data packets sent regularly. Server-side dashboard updates reflect local device stats. |
| **OTA Trigger** | Device suspends tasks, shows update progress on OLED, and reboots into new firmware. |

---

## 3. Full Testing Checklist

### Section A: Boot & Network
- [ ] **Startup**: Power on via USB/Battery. Verify OLED turns on and pet appears.
- [ ] **Provisioning**: (If fresh) Verify AP "Kaku-Pet-Setup" exists. Connect and save credentials.
- [ ] **Reconnection**: Turn off WiFi router. Verify device handles disconnect and reconnects once router is back.

### Section B: Interface & Animations
- [ ] **Menu Entry**: Hold device tilted RIGHT for 2 seconds. Verify Menu Icons appear.
- [ ] **Menu Navigation**: Flick device RIGHT while in menu. Verify icons cycle (Food -> Toilet -> Play -> Health -> Info).
- [ ] **Animation Continuity**: Observe Child and Adult animations. Verify no "flicker" or "blank frames".

### Section C: Sensors & Input
- [ ] **Orientation Sleep**: Place device neutral for 2 minutes. Verify it enters low-power/sleep mode.
- [ ] **Motion Wake**: Shake the device while sleeping. Verify it wakes up and returns to idle.
- [ ] **Feeding Gesture**: Select Food Menu -> Tilt Left Hold. Verify "Eating" animation plays.
- [ ] **Cleaning Gesture**: Select Toilet Menu -> Tilt Left Hold. Verify "Cleaning" animation plays (Brushing).
- [ ] **Step Counter**: Walk with the device or shake it. Verify step count increments on the Info page.

### Section D: Server & Data
- [ ] **Data Upload**: Check [Web Dashboard](file:///f:/kakuProject-main/index.html). Verify Hunger/Health stats match device levels.
- [ ] **Image Capture**: Perform Feeding action. Verify an image appears in the "Latest Camera" section of the dashboard.
- [ ] **AI Captioning**: Verify the BLIP model generates a valid caption (e.g., "A tray of sushi") after feeding.
- [ ] **Event Polling**: Change pet emotion from the dashboard. Verify the device switches animation accordingly.

---

## 4. Bug Detection Hints

| Failure Symptom | Possible Cause |
| :--- | :--- |
| **OLED stuck on "Connecting..."** | Incorrect WiFi credentials or server address in firmware. |
| **Pet doesn't age or get hungry** | `PHYSIO_TICK_MS` logic failing or timer not running on Core 1. |
| **Menu won't open on tilt** | MPU6050 I2C communication error or calibration drift. |
| **Animations playing too fast** | Frame delay constants in [oledTask](file:///f:/kakuProject-main/esp32_sketch/esp32_sketch.ino#1091-1104) set too low. |
| **Server shows "No Data"** | API key mismatch or firewall blocking HTTPS requests. |
| **Camera image is green/corrupt** | Flash size / PSRAM settings in Arduino IDE (should be 8MB OPI). |
| **UI freezes during action** | Network task (Core 1) blocking Core 0, or I2C bus collision. |

---

## 5. Success Criteria
*   [ ] Device survives 24h without crash.
*   [ ] Stats correctly reflect the care provided (Hunger 0 when fed, Health 100 when clean).
*   [ ] All 4 life stages (Infant, Child, Adult, Old) cycle correctly based on Uptime.
*   [ ] AI Vision generates accurate captions for food items.
